<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">combat</ansi>

Combat in DOGMud features a tactical, skill-based system with layered
defenses, special moves, and resource management.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Starting Combat ━━━</ansi>

Use <ansi fg="command">attack <target></ansi> to engage. Once started, combat
continues each round until someone flees or dies.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Attack Mechanics ━━━</ansi>

Your attack success is based on:
  - <ansi fg="stat">Combat Skill:</ansi> Weapon, Unarmed, or Ranged Combat
  - <ansi fg="stat">Dexterity:</ansi> Affects accuracy and swing count
  - <ansi fg="stat">Stamina:</ansi> Low stamina reduces hit chance and damage

<ansi fg="red">Critical Hits:</ansi> Skill advantage increases crit chance
<ansi fg="red">Fumbles:</ansi> Even skilled attacks can go badly wrong

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Unarmed Combat ━━━</ansi>

Fighting with fists, claws, or bare hands:
  - <ansi fg="stat">Both Hands:</ansi> Attack with all empty hands (up to 6 fists
    with extra arms mutation)
  - <ansi fg="stat">Fist/Claws Weapons:</ansi> Count as unarmed, train the skill
  - <ansi fg="stat">Speed Bonus:</ansi> Faster attack speed than armed fighters
  - <ansi fg="stat">No Parry:</ansi> Can only dodge, no weapon to deflect with
  - <ansi fg="stat">No Penalty:</ansi> Natural weapons ignore dual-wield penalty
  - <ansi fg="stat">Mixed Setup:</ansi> Sword in one hand + empty hand still
    punches with the free hand
  - <ansi fg="stat">Grapple Advantage:</ansi> Fists and claws fit comfortably
    in any grapple, and long weapons lose effectiveness in close
    quarters. See <ansi fg="command">help grapple</ansi>.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Layered Defense System ━━━</ansi>

When attacked, all available defenses are rolled simultaneously.
The defense that wins by the widest margin is used:

  1. <ansi fg="stat">Dodge:</ansi> Unarmed Combat + Dexterity
     - Available to everyone
  2. <ansi fg="stat">Parry:</ansi> Weapon Combat + weapon parry rating
     - Requires a weapon (not fists/claws)
  3. <ansi fg="stat">Block:</ansi> Weapon Combat + shield block rating
     - Requires a shield equipped
  4. <ansi fg="stat">Quell:</ansi> Willpower + Spellcasting, against spells that
     attack the mind. Costs conviction.
  5. <ansi fg="stat">Defy:</ansi> Willpower + Rhetoric, against taunts. Costs
     conviction.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Defense Crits ━━━</ansi>

A rare, exceptional defense -- reading the attack almost before it lands --
triggers a powerful counter-move against the attacker:

  <ansi fg="cyan-bold">⚔ Parry Crit → RIPOSTE:</ansi> Free counter-attack with reduced damage.
    Your blade turns their strike aside and bites back.
  <ansi fg="cyan-bold">⚡ Dodge Crit → SWEEP:</ansi> Automatic trip attempt (ignores
    cooldown). Dodge under their swing and sweep their legs.
  <ansi fg="cyan-bold">🛡 Block Crit → SHIELD SLAM:</ansi> Automatic bash attempt
    (ignores cooldown). Catch the blow and slam them back.

A defence that succeeds without being exceptional still helps: it takes the
force out of the blow rather than stopping it outright. The crits above are
the top of that range, when a defence goes perfectly.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Dual Wielding ━━━</ansi>

Wield two weapons for extra attacks, but with tradeoffs:
  - <ansi fg="stat">Extra Attacks:</ansi> Offhand weapon gets reduced swing count
  - <ansi fg="stat">Accuracy Penalty:</ansi> Reduced hit chance (scales with skill)
  - <ansi fg="stat">Skill Progression:</ansi> Each weapon trains its own skill
  - <ansi fg="stat">Defense:</ansi> Can parry with either weapon

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Special Combat Moves ━━━</ansi>

Tactical moves with cooldowns that can turn the tide:

  <ansi fg="command">bash</ansi>    - Shield strike with a chance to knock down
  <ansi fg="command">trip</ansi>    - Reliable leg sweep with light damage
  <ansi fg="command">kick</ansi>    - Strong strike with a chance to knock down
  <ansi fg="command">taunt</ansi>   - Verbal assault (conviction damage)
  <ansi fg="command">grapple</ansi> - Grabs and restrains an opponent.

All share the special-move cooldown. Knockdowns apply prone.

Submissions (joint locks, chokes) fire automatically when you
decisively win a grapple round from a dominant position. See
<ansi fg="command">help submission</ansi>.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Target Switching ━━━</ansi>

  - Use <ansi fg="command">attack <new-target></ansi> to retarget mid-combat
  - Free switch when your current target is dead or gone
  - Contested switch against a living target costs a round

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Resource Management ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="stat">Stamina:</ansi> Fuels attacks, physical defenses, ranged
    actions, special moves, fleeing, and grapple upkeep.
  <ansi fg="stat">Conviction:</ansi> Fuels spells, rhetoric actions, quell,
    and defy, and is attacked by taunts.
  <ansi fg="stat">Health:</ansi> Reach 0 and you die, then wake at safety

For physical actions, load raises the price while the governing skill lowers
it. Governing skill also lowers the price of acts of will. Voluntary actions
require full payment and refuse before their effects if you cannot pay.

Autoattacks, the winning defense, flee, and ongoing grapple maintenance are
never refused for shortage. They spend what remains and resolve in a desperate
form without the governing skill. Losing defense choices cost nothing and say
nothing.

